# A quick turn of PRESET: input() runs between frames, so several detents can come between two audio blocks, each a whole piece's worth of commands. Whatever the
# moment, nothing is lost that matters: an autosave's fade cancelled by the turn does not leave it mute, and the project and the engine end up agreeing on every value
# (enagree counts what they disagree on). Every case is run at six offsets, because a block is 5.8 ms and "turn PRESET n 1" is n ms: the same moves at each place in it.
wait 3000
# ---- resting, a knob, the autosave's fade under way, two detents: the fade is cancelled and the sound comes back
tap PLAY
wait 200
expect playing 0
# offset 0
wait 0
spin K2 1
wait 4030
expect saving 1
turn PRESET 2 1
wait 60
expect saving 0
expect ducked 0
expect enagree 0
peakreset
wait 500
expect ducked 0
expect peak_db_max >-40
# offset 1
wait 1
spin K2 1
wait 4030
expect saving 1
turn PRESET -2 1
wait 60
expect saving 0
expect ducked 0
expect enagree 0
peakreset
wait 500
expect ducked 0
expect peak_db_max >-40
# offset 2
wait 2
spin K2 1
wait 4030
expect saving 1
turn PRESET 2 1
wait 60
expect saving 0
expect ducked 0
expect enagree 0
peakreset
wait 500
expect ducked 0
expect peak_db_max >-40
# offset 3
wait 3
spin K2 1
wait 4030
expect saving 1
turn PRESET -2 1
wait 60
expect saving 0
expect ducked 0
expect enagree 0
peakreset
wait 500
expect ducked 0
expect peak_db_max >-40
# offset 4
wait 4
spin K2 1
wait 4030
expect saving 1
turn PRESET 2 1
wait 60
expect saving 0
expect ducked 0
expect enagree 0
peakreset
wait 500
expect ducked 0
expect peak_db_max >-40
# offset 5
wait 5
spin K2 1
wait 4030
expect saving 1
turn PRESET -2 1
wait 60
expect saving 0
expect ducked 0
expect enagree 0
peakreset
wait 500
expect ducked 0
expect peak_db_max >-40
tap PLAY
wait 200
expect playing 1
# ---- two and three detents in a gap, from a piece in Auto to pieces in Hands and back: the mode goes with the last piece
press SEL
tap HOME
release SEL
wait 100
expect piece 0
expect arrange 0
expect mode 0
# offset 0: 2 detents, and back
turn PRESET 2 1
wait 30
expect piece 2
expect arrange 1
expect mode 1
expect enagree 0
turn PRESET -2 1
wait 30
expect piece 0
expect arrange 0
expect mode 0
expect enagree 0
# offset 1: 3 detents, and back
turn PRESET 3 1
wait 31
expect piece 3
expect arrange 1
expect mode 1
expect enagree 0
turn PRESET -3 1
wait 31
expect piece 0
expect arrange 0
expect mode 0
expect enagree 0
# offset 2: 2 detents, and back
turn PRESET 2 1
wait 32
expect piece 2
expect arrange 1
expect mode 1
expect enagree 0
turn PRESET -2 1
wait 32
expect piece 0
expect arrange 0
expect mode 0
expect enagree 0
# offset 3: 3 detents, and back
turn PRESET 3 1
wait 33
expect piece 3
expect arrange 1
expect mode 1
expect enagree 0
turn PRESET -3 1
wait 33
expect piece 0
expect arrange 0
expect mode 0
expect enagree 0
# offset 4: 2 detents, and back
turn PRESET 2 1
wait 34
expect piece 2
expect arrange 1
expect mode 1
expect enagree 0
turn PRESET -2 1
wait 34
expect piece 0
expect arrange 0
expect mode 0
expect enagree 0
# offset 5: 3 detents, and back
turn PRESET 3 1
wait 35
expect piece 3
expect arrange 1
expect mode 1
expect enagree 0
turn PRESET -3 1
wait 35
expect piece 0
expect arrange 0
expect mode 0
expect enagree 0
# ---- a whole quick turn: the last piece, whatever the gaps
turn PRESET 7 2
wait 50
expect piece 7
expect enagree 0
turn PRESET 1 1
wait 50
expect piece 0
expect enagree 0
# the piece is still heard as the piece: the seed moved, the card says it
expect screen 4
# ---- a piece, then SAVE held back to the recipe in the same breath: the recipe, in the engine too
spin K2 3
turn PRESET 2 1
press SAVE
wait 1600
release SAVE
wait 50
expect enagree 0
# ---- a knob turned while a piece waits for room: the knob's value stays
turn PRESET 3 1
spin K1 2
wait 50
expect enagree 0
# ---- more than the queue holds of anything: dropped values come back once there is room, not on the next change. Nothing is left to the next write
flood 200
wait 60
expect enagree 0
flood 200
turn PRESET 1 1
wait 60
expect enagree 0
wait 5000
expect ducked 0
# ---- the last piece of a quick turn has its own seed, as any piece has: nothing of its tail is lost (the simulator's seed: 7 + 1009 for each piece since the start)
reboot
wait 200
expect seed 7
turn PRESET 2 1
wait 50
expect seed 2025
reboot
wait 203
turn PRESET 3 1
wait 50
expect seed 3034
reboot
wait 205
turn PRESET 3 1
wait 50
expect seed 3034
